WEBVTT

00:00:21.520 --> 00:00:23.700
Wow!  You actually built it!

00:00:24.100 --> 00:00:30.170
By increasing Moment's rotation radius, 
we increased its output by 150%.

00:00:30.740 --> 00:00:33.640
It's due to our company's newest techniques.

00:00:34.390 --> 00:00:39.150
We already installed Yusei 
and Bruno's revised program.

00:00:39.890 --> 00:00:42.660
This is the result of the simulation test.

00:00:43.820 --> 00:00:47.460
We can now use our program 
to its fullest potential.

00:00:48.990 --> 00:00:51.400
You're really doing this for us?

00:00:51.400 --> 00:00:54.480
Since your president was arrested, 
aren't you having tough times?

00:00:54.480 --> 00:00:57.970
Yes.  Due to that incident, no one 
wants to work with our company.

00:00:58.600 --> 00:01:04.170
But the president wanted 
to make amends with you.

00:01:04.170 --> 00:01:06.510
You're not firing Bolger?

00:01:06.510 --> 00:01:08.440
He won't be out for awhile.

00:01:09.160 --> 00:01:15.420
It's true that the president committed a 
crime, but none of the employees hate him.

00:01:16.420 --> 00:01:21.220
Everyone knows that the president 
truly loved D-Wheels.

00:01:22.760 --> 00:01:27.900
We'll protect this company until 
he finishes atoning for the past.

00:01:28.140 --> 00:01:29.160
I see.

00:01:29.160 --> 00:01:30.940
Thank you, Rick.

00:01:30.940 --> 00:01:33.940
We're now much closer 
to fulfilling our dream.

00:01:47.680 --> 00:01:49.150
Yusei!

00:01:49.630 --> 00:01:52.560
Is it true that the new D-Wheels are ready?

00:01:52.560 --> 00:01:53.980
Yeah, it's true.

00:01:53.980 --> 00:01:54.620
Huh?

00:01:55.780 --> 00:01:58.830
We also have new riding suits.

00:01:58.830 --> 00:02:00.600
Looks good, right?

00:02:03.720 --> 00:02:05.030
Anyone can look good with the right clothes.

00:02:05.410 --> 00:02:10.200
It would be pathetic if you wore your usual 
shabby clothes on the brightest stage.

00:02:10.200 --> 00:02:13.710
Stop being arrogant when you 
always wear the same clothes!

00:02:13.710 --> 00:02:16.510
Unlike your clothes, mine is a riding suit!

00:02:17.920 --> 00:02:19.480
5D's?

00:02:19.970 --> 00:02:21.580
Is this the team name?

00:02:21.580 --> 00:02:22.450
Yeah.

00:02:22.780 --> 00:02:25.850
Jack chose the name without us.

00:02:25.850 --> 00:02:30.190
It's much better than your idea: The 
Fountain Courtyard Friendly Alliance.

00:02:30.680 --> 00:02:32.930
What does 5D's mean?

00:02:33.240 --> 00:02:35.760
Since it's 5D's, there are five Ds.

00:02:35.760 --> 00:02:37.930
Umm, D for Devil.

00:02:37.930 --> 00:02:39.150
D for Destroy.

00:02:39.150 --> 00:02:40.600
D for Dead Heat.

00:02:40.600 --> 00:02:41.610
D for Dark.

00:02:41.610 --> 00:02:43.070
And umm...

00:02:43.500 --> 00:02:45.940
D for Daisuki Bruno?(Note: 
Daisuki means Love.)

00:02:46.670 --> 00:02:47.670
I was only kidding.

00:02:48.240 --> 00:02:50.140
5D's is this!

00:02:50.560 --> 00:02:53.110
The five marks of the Crimson Dragon.

00:02:53.420 --> 00:02:54.220
That's right.

00:02:54.740 --> 00:02:59.080
The mark of the Crimson 
Dragon forged our bond.

00:02:59.440 --> 00:03:06.350
I don't have a mark, but Luca's mark 
was the reason I met all of you.

00:03:07.180 --> 00:03:09.400
You and Luca together count as one person.

00:03:10.500 --> 00:03:12.660
My name isn't included!

00:03:13.070 --> 00:03:15.630
Let's name the team" Bruno and 5D's!"

00:03:16.760 --> 00:03:18.870
I said I was kidding.

00:03:19.520 --> 00:03:21.790
I think it's an excellent name.

00:03:21.790 --> 00:03:22.340
Yeah.

00:03:25.390 --> 00:03:28.900
Starting today, we're Team 5D's!

00:03:47.930 --> 00:03:53.300
Every time you're hurt, you can become kinder

00:03:53.300 --> 00:03:58.840
Stand up and you'll understand strength

00:03:58.840 --> 00:04:03.420
Don't look back and keep going

00:04:03.420 --> 00:04:09.080
Both the past and the future 
are connected to the present

00:04:09.080 --> 00:04:14.120
There's no need to fear

00:04:14.120 --> 00:04:21.760
I'll keep telling you that you're not alone

00:04:22.630 --> 00:04:27.900
The passionate emotions in your heart

00:04:28.300 --> 00:04:33.540
Streak to the infinite future

00:04:33.540 --> 00:04:39.130
Dreams surpass their limits

00:04:39.130 --> 00:04:47.050
And will lead you to a bright place

00:05:12.950 --> 00:05:18.720
Formed!  Team 5D's

00:05:27.360 --> 00:05:30.040
They've made the matchups 
for the preliminaries?

00:05:30.060 --> 00:05:30.630
Yeah.

00:05:31.050 --> 00:05:33.240
The preliminaries are in league format.

00:05:33.240 --> 00:05:35.600
32 teams are participating.

00:05:35.960 --> 00:05:40.190
They're divided into eight blocks, and they 
battle in league format in each block.

00:05:40.190 --> 00:05:44.520
The top two teams in each 
block make the finals.

00:05:44.520 --> 00:05:47.580
The surviving teams battle 
in tournament format.

00:05:47.870 --> 00:05:53.710
Since there are four teams per block, we 
can advance to the finals if we win twice.

00:05:53.710 --> 00:05:59.790
Hey, is our first opponent Team Unicorn?

00:05:59.790 --> 00:06:01.760
Team Unicorn?

00:06:01.760 --> 00:06:04.730
We met them at the tournament party.

00:06:04.730 --> 00:06:06.770
Oh yeah!  Them!

00:06:08.590 --> 00:06:11.770
Team Unicorn won the Atlantis Tournament.

00:06:12.320 --> 00:06:15.740
They're said to be frontrunners 
for winning this tournament.

00:06:16.980 --> 00:06:20.800
I wish they didn't put 
that team in our block.

00:06:21.680 --> 00:06:24.060
It doesn't matter if they're 
tournament favorites.

00:06:24.060 --> 00:06:27.220
We'll crush everyone who stand in our way!

00:06:27.860 --> 00:06:29.580
Jack is right.

00:06:29.580 --> 00:06:33.630
If our goal is to win the tournament, we'll 
eventually have to battle against powerful teams.

00:06:33.630 --> 00:06:36.190
It's just a matter of when.

00:06:36.450 --> 00:06:39.170
That's true, but...

00:06:39.170 --> 00:06:41.930
Yusei, it's time for practice.

00:06:42.240 --> 00:06:44.810
Right.  Crow and Jack, let's go.

00:06:45.900 --> 00:06:48.120
What's practice?

00:06:48.120 --> 00:06:49.870
It's a practice run.

00:06:49.870 --> 00:06:51.980
Let's watch from the stands.

00:06:56.420 --> 00:07:00.860
Team 5D's will now use 
this lane for practice.

00:07:00.860 --> 00:07:03.950
All other teams are prohibited from using it.

00:07:03.950 --> 00:07:04.720
{missing?}

00:07:05.140 --> 00:07:07.530
Is that...

00:07:09.400 --> 00:07:10.970
Ushio!

00:07:11.920 --> 00:07:13.900
It's you guys.

00:07:13.900 --> 00:07:15.600
Did you come to cheer for Yusei?

00:07:15.600 --> 00:07:16.600
Yeah.

00:07:16.600 --> 00:07:19.660
Why are you dressed like that?

00:07:19.660 --> 00:07:21.240
Look for yourself.

00:07:21.890 --> 00:07:25.230
Even though each team is 
scheduled at a different time,

00:07:25.230 --> 00:07:27.710
all the duel lanes are 
still full for practice.

00:07:28.290 --> 00:07:33.850
Autopilot isn't allowed in this 
tournament, so there are many accidents.

00:07:33.850 --> 00:07:38.820
They recruited me to work because they 
don't have enough people to help.

00:07:39.440 --> 00:07:40.750
I see.

00:07:40.750 --> 00:07:43.110
Look!  Yusei is coming out!

00:07:57.990 --> 00:07:59.070
That's good acceleration!

00:07:59.490 --> 00:08:01.310
The power is much greater than before!

00:08:01.880 --> 00:08:03.050
It feels good!

00:08:11.000 --> 00:08:13.080
Pearson...  Bolger...

00:08:13.080 --> 00:08:16.560
The Blackbird you built is now very fast.

00:08:17.190 --> 00:08:21.480
I promise to win the WRGP for you!

00:08:21.480 --> 00:08:25.330
Let's use them to their maximum potential!

00:08:31.100 --> 00:08:33.420
They seem to be doing well.

00:08:33.420 --> 00:08:36.620
Yeah.  It's because we 
revamped their engines.

00:08:36.620 --> 00:08:39.080
It's on a different level 
than the previous vehicles.

00:08:40.480 --> 00:08:43.080
I'm looking forward to battling them again.

00:08:43.500 --> 00:08:45.160
Battle them again?

00:08:45.800 --> 00:08:49.060
Well, I'll patrol somewhere else.

00:08:50.520 --> 00:08:52.700
Say hi to Yusei for me.

00:08:53.330 --> 00:08:57.030
Ushio, are you also 
participating in the WRGP?

00:08:57.960 --> 00:09:00.800
That's a secret.  See ya!

00:09:09.240 --> 00:09:12.410
Team 5D's, your practice time is almost over.

00:09:12.840 --> 00:09:14.110
You heard the announcement.

00:09:14.110 --> 00:09:17.230
Jack and Crow, let's leave 
the course during this lap.

00:09:17.230 --> 00:09:22.040
I'm going to make another lap because 
the next team won't show up immediately!

00:09:22.040 --> 00:09:22.890
Hey Crow!

00:09:23.200 --> 00:09:25.360
He's so selfish!

00:09:29.060 --> 00:09:31.530
I'm addicted to this power!

00:09:37.280 --> 00:09:38.180
Oh no!

00:09:45.470 --> 00:09:46.320
What?

00:09:46.320 --> 00:09:47.280
What happened?

00:09:47.280 --> 00:09:48.910
It looks like an accident.

00:09:52.480 --> 00:09:53.480
Oh no!

00:09:55.540 --> 00:09:56.760
Are you okay, Breo?

00:09:57.510 --> 00:09:58.960
Are you hurt?

00:09:58.960 --> 00:10:01.090
I'm fine, Andore.

00:10:01.690 --> 00:10:04.330
I'm sorry!  Are you hurt?

00:10:04.330 --> 00:10:06.280
What's up with you?

00:10:06.280 --> 00:10:07.570
What do you mean?

00:10:07.960 --> 00:10:09.240
It wasn't on purpose.

00:10:09.240 --> 00:10:11.500
Whatever!  I don't believe you!

00:10:11.500 --> 00:10:12.040
Stop it!

00:10:12.480 --> 00:10:14.110
He said that it wasn't on purpose!

00:10:14.730 --> 00:10:18.460
Oh really?  It's currently our practice time.

00:10:18.460 --> 00:10:20.480
It's strange that you're still riding.

00:10:20.900 --> 00:10:22.420
That's true, but...

00:10:23.000 --> 00:10:24.300
We're very sorry.

00:10:24.300 --> 00:10:26.680
It's our fault for not being careful.

00:10:26.680 --> 00:10:27.950
We won't make excuses.

00:10:28.880 --> 00:10:32.160
Many people want to hinder us.

00:10:32.160 --> 00:10:35.280
We'll talk to the committee so that 
you can't enter the preliminaries!

00:10:35.280 --> 00:10:36.440
Stop it, Jan!

00:10:36.440 --> 00:10:38.900
It's not worth it to win like that!

00:10:39.270 --> 00:10:40.360
Preliminaries?

00:10:40.360 --> 00:10:43.370
Did you forget our faces, Yusei Fudo?

00:10:46.450 --> 00:10:47.300
You're...

00:10:48.470 --> 00:10:49.370
Team Unicorn!

00:10:51.960 --> 00:10:53.560
You remembered.

00:10:53.560 --> 00:10:56.580
I'm surprised that we would meet again here.

00:10:56.580 --> 00:10:58.010
I'm Andore.

00:10:58.010 --> 00:10:59.540
This is Jan.

00:10:59.540 --> 00:11:00.960
And Breo.

00:11:00.960 --> 00:11:02.050
Hello.

00:11:03.710 --> 00:11:05.980
I'm sorry.  Are you okay?

00:11:05.980 --> 00:11:08.460
Yeah.  That was a good hit.

00:11:09.520 --> 00:11:11.140
Those words hurt.

00:11:11.590 --> 00:11:15.630
Anyway, look at what 
happened to your D-Wheel.

00:11:16.150 --> 00:11:18.760
Don't worry about it.

00:11:18.760 --> 00:11:20.400
We have plenty of spares.

00:11:21.430 --> 00:11:24.110
Thankfully, the sponsors love us.

00:11:24.110 --> 00:11:25.240
Don't worry about it.

00:11:25.240 --> 00:11:28.080
No way!  Let me pay!

00:11:28.850 --> 00:11:31.770
Take it easy.  I know that 
you don't have any money.

00:11:31.770 --> 00:11:33.550
Stop it, Jan.  You're going too far.

00:11:34.630 --> 00:11:36.750
It's frustrating, but I 
can't say anything back.

00:11:37.150 --> 00:11:41.400
But we're not satisfied 
because it's all our fault.

00:11:41.400 --> 00:11:44.460
Then how about this?

00:11:44.960 --> 00:11:50.430
You'll battle us now.  If you win, you 
don't have to pay for the damages.

00:11:50.760 --> 00:11:51.530
What?

00:11:51.900 --> 00:11:55.580
This course is currently reserved 
for Team Unicorn's practice time.

00:11:55.580 --> 00:11:59.020
There's no problem if 
we duel during our time.

00:11:59.020 --> 00:12:00.410
Stop it, Andore.

00:12:00.410 --> 00:12:02.700
It's a waste of time to battle them.

00:12:02.700 --> 00:12:05.870
We don't have time to battle all three.

00:12:05.870 --> 00:12:08.020
How about a one-on-one battle 
between me and Yusei?

00:12:08.600 --> 00:12:09.480
Me?

00:12:09.970 --> 00:12:12.060
You intrigue me.

00:12:12.060 --> 00:12:15.460
Show me the skills that won the Fortune Cup.

00:12:16.500 --> 00:12:18.830
Sounds fun!  Do it, Yusei!

00:12:18.830 --> 00:12:20.930
But we're facing them in the preliminaries.

00:12:21.340 --> 00:12:22.680
That's right, Yusei.

00:12:22.680 --> 00:12:24.970
There's no need to show them our hand.

00:12:24.970 --> 00:12:26.900
We don't need to accept this battle.

00:12:27.260 --> 00:12:28.800
That's right, Andore.

00:12:28.800 --> 00:12:32.120
There's no benefit in 
defeating these no-names.

00:12:32.120 --> 00:12:32.910
Say what?

00:12:32.910 --> 00:12:36.380
Isn't that right, former King Jack Atlas?

00:12:36.380 --> 00:12:37.660
How dare you!

00:12:37.660 --> 00:12:41.850
You know that I'm Jack Atlas, but you still 
called me a no-name?  That's unforgivable!

00:12:41.850 --> 00:12:45.140
Yusei, accept this battle!

00:12:46.810 --> 00:12:51.290
Fine.  If it'll satisfy 
you, I accept this battle.

00:12:51.600 --> 00:12:53.340
That's the spirit!

00:13:07.520 --> 00:13:09.940
Speed World 2 set on.

00:13:13.960 --> 00:13:16.880
The first step worked.

00:13:16.880 --> 00:13:19.600
It was hard to fall so spectacularly.

00:13:19.600 --> 00:13:21.390
Sorry, Breo.

00:13:21.390 --> 00:13:26.060
But thanks to you, they 
accepted our Riding Duel.

00:13:26.060 --> 00:13:31.160
But was it worth wrecking a D-Wheel for them?

00:13:31.160 --> 00:13:37.080
If I'm correct, they're our 
greatest rivals in the WRGP.

00:13:37.080 --> 00:13:41.500
They don't suspect that it was all an act.

00:13:41.500 --> 00:13:43.040
Good.

00:13:43.500 --> 00:13:47.310
The preliminary battles have already started.

00:13:47.690 --> 00:13:51.510
Let's observe their skills.

00:13:54.030 --> 00:13:56.750
Riding Duel!  Acceleration!

00:14:00.590 --> 00:14:04.140
I can see why he's Team Unicorn's 
ace.  He had a good start.

00:14:04.140 --> 00:14:04.910
However...

00:14:06.240 --> 00:14:08.430
My engine starts powering up!

00:14:14.340 --> 00:14:16.270
All right!  That's a good start!

00:14:16.270 --> 00:14:17.810
He gets to go first!

00:14:18.680 --> 00:14:21.610
It powers up at that moment.  
That's a good engine.

00:14:21.610 --> 00:14:26.900
Yes, but I told Andore to 
keep the throttle at 80%.

00:14:30.240 --> 00:14:35.220
Jan ordered me to let Yusei go first 
so that we can witness his skills.

00:14:35.720 --> 00:14:38.760
Let me see your skills, Yusei Fudo.

00:14:42.630 --> 00:14:44.630
Here I go!  My turn!

00:14:46.030 --> 00:14:48.140
I summon Max Warrior!

00:14:52.140 --> 00:14:54.210
I end my turn.

00:14:55.200 --> 00:14:57.550
That's it?

00:14:57.550 --> 00:15:01.580
He has the same idea as us and 
wants to see what we'll do.

00:15:01.950 --> 00:15:04.410
Which deck did you give Andore?

00:15:04.410 --> 00:15:06.240
It's the quick attack power deck.

00:15:06.240 --> 00:15:10.650
Not only is it easy to understand, but 
it'll also leave a lasting impression.

00:15:10.650 --> 00:15:15.060
Only Andore can expertly 
use that difficult deck.

00:15:15.470 --> 00:15:20.720
In a real duel, you won't always get the 
cards you need to execute your strategy.

00:15:20.720 --> 00:15:24.670
The six random cards you draw 
can determine victory or defeat.

00:15:24.670 --> 00:15:28.040
That's when your card playing 
skills become important.

00:15:28.660 --> 00:15:34.510
Andore has first-rate card playing skills, 
so he always finds the best strategy

00:15:34.510 --> 00:15:37.750
among the cards he's drawn.

00:15:38.160 --> 00:15:40.520
He's a natural talent.

00:15:42.140 --> 00:15:45.840
If you're not going to attack me, 
then I'm going to attack you.

00:15:45.840 --> 00:15:47.180
My turn!

00:15:48.870 --> 00:15:51.340
I summon Playful Possum!

00:15:54.560 --> 00:15:57.450
I activate Playful Possum's effect!

00:15:57.450 --> 00:16:04.570
If you have a monster with higher 
attack points, I can destroy my card!

00:16:05.620 --> 00:16:06.700
Fake Die!

00:16:08.610 --> 00:16:09.580
What?

00:16:09.580 --> 00:16:13.550
Huh?  He destroyed his own card.

00:16:14.610 --> 00:16:17.790
Andore is already planning 
to execute that combo.

00:16:18.010 --> 00:16:23.610
Due to its destruction, I can Special Summon 
Green Baboon, Defender of the Forest from my hand!

00:16:28.940 --> 00:16:33.070
When a Beast-Type monster 
on my field is destroyed...

00:16:33.070 --> 00:16:36.970
I can Special Summon Green Baboon from 
my hand by paying 1000 life points!

00:16:37.330 --> 00:16:39.390
Now I understand.

00:16:39.390 --> 00:16:43.450
You destroyed your monster so that you 
can quickly summon a high Level monster.

00:16:43.710 --> 00:16:46.970
Go, Green Baboon!  Attack Max Warrior!

00:16:46.970 --> 00:16:48.570
Hammer Club Death!

00:16:53.280 --> 00:16:54.250
Yusei!

00:16:54.250 --> 00:16:55.330
That guy fights well.

00:16:55.680 --> 00:16:58.820
I set two cards and end my turn!

00:16:59.260 --> 00:17:00.480
My turn!

00:17:02.540 --> 00:17:06.270
I activate Speed Spell - 
Angel Baton from my hand!

00:17:06.270 --> 00:17:11.430
When I have two or more Speed Counters, 
I draw two cards from my deck.

00:17:12.250 --> 00:17:14.550
Then I send one card in 
my hand to the graveyard!

00:17:15.880 --> 00:17:18.780
I activate another Angel Baton!

00:17:19.160 --> 00:17:20.620
Double Speed Spells!

00:17:20.880 --> 00:17:22.520
That's clever.

00:17:24.400 --> 00:17:27.060
I summon Junk Synchron!

00:17:31.600 --> 00:17:37.300
When I successfully summon this card, I can Special 
Summon a Level 2-or-below monster from my graveyard!

00:17:38.000 --> 00:17:40.520
Appear, Speed Warrior!

00:17:44.170 --> 00:17:50.060
When a Tuner Monster is on my field, I can 
Special Summon Quillbolt Hedgehog from my graveyard!

00:17:53.920 --> 00:17:58.620
He Special Summoned the two monsters that he 
discarded to pay for the double Speed Spells.

00:17:59.100 --> 00:18:00.780
He doesn't waste anything during a duel.

00:18:00.780 --> 00:18:04.910
Yusei Fudo is a duelist who 
lives up to his reputation.

00:18:04.910 --> 00:18:07.580
Hey, this isn't the time to admire him.

00:18:07.580 --> 00:18:09.600
This is how he typically wins.

00:18:10.740 --> 00:18:12.070
Do you think so?

00:18:12.300 --> 00:18:19.040
Level 3 Junk Synchron tunes Level 2 
Quillbolt Hedgehog and Level 2 Speed Warrior!

00:18:25.150 --> 00:18:28.890
The roars come together to form an 
echoing arrow that pierces the sky!

00:18:28.890 --> 00:18:30.690
Become the path that lights the way!

00:18:30.690 --> 00:18:32.120
Synchro Summon!

00:18:32.120 --> 00:18:33.850
Come, Junk Archer!

00:18:35.370 --> 00:18:37.290
I activate Junk Archer's effect!

00:18:37.800 --> 00:18:43.030
Once per turn, Junk Archer can remove 
a monster on your field from play!

00:18:43.610 --> 00:18:45.100
Dimension Shoot!

00:18:47.830 --> 00:18:50.600
He doesn't have any monsters on his field!

00:18:50.600 --> 00:18:53.340
Go, Yusei!  Attack him directly!

00:18:53.340 --> 00:18:55.580
Junk Archer attacks you directly!

00:18:55.980 --> 00:18:57.540
Scrap Arrow!

00:18:58.780 --> 00:19:01.540
I won't let your attack succeed so easily!

00:19:01.990 --> 00:19:03.850
I activate the trap Battle Instinct!

00:19:04.310 --> 00:19:10.590
When I take a direct attack, I can Special 
Summon a Level 4-or-below monster from my hand!

00:19:11.440 --> 00:19:14.290
I call forth Nimble Momonga!

00:19:18.200 --> 00:19:18.730
What?

00:19:23.680 --> 00:19:25.670
Yusei has taken the lead!

00:19:25.950 --> 00:19:29.800
But at this moment, Nimble 
Momonga's effect activates!

00:19:29.800 --> 00:19:34.650
When Nimble Momonga is sent to the graveyard 
due to battle, I regain 1000 life points!

00:19:34.940 --> 00:19:39.550
Then I can Special Summon two cards 
with the same name in defense position!

00:19:43.120 --> 00:19:46.000
I set one card and end my turn.

00:19:46.920 --> 00:19:51.130
Green Baboon, which was removed from 
play due to Junk Archer's effect,

00:19:51.130 --> 00:19:53.300
returns at the End Phase.

00:19:55.290 --> 00:19:58.400
Wasn't Yusei supposed to be in the lead?

00:19:58.400 --> 00:20:00.940
He hasn't lost that many life points,

00:20:01.310 --> 00:20:03.910
and he also has three monsters on his field.

00:20:04.170 --> 00:20:07.880
Yusei is at a total disadvantage 
at the end of the turn!

00:20:08.120 --> 00:20:09.610
Andore is doing well.

00:20:09.610 --> 00:20:13.850
Yeah.  It's his natural 
card playing instincts.

00:20:14.400 --> 00:20:16.920
Yusei, you attacked carelessly.

00:20:17.470 --> 00:20:19.580
Your card playing skills have flaws.

00:20:19.580 --> 00:20:21.160
Here I go!  My turn!

00:20:22.470 --> 00:20:24.620
I activate Playful Possum's effect!

00:20:24.620 --> 00:20:26.940
When Playful Possum's own effect 
puts it in the graveyard,

00:20:26.940 --> 00:20:29.670
I can Special Summon it 
during the Standby Phase!

00:20:30.830 --> 00:20:32.630
Resurrect, Playful Possum!

00:20:33.550 --> 00:20:40.380
I tribute Playful Possum and Nimble Momonga to 
Tribute Summon Behemoth the King of All Animals!

00:20:50.570 --> 00:20:52.020
Behemoth?

00:20:52.680 --> 00:20:56.160
I activate Behemoth's effect!

00:20:56.160 --> 00:20:58.760
When Behemoth is successfully 
Tribute Summoned...

00:20:58.760 --> 00:21:00.700
I can return the same number 
of Beast-Type monsters

00:21:00.700 --> 00:21:04.000
in my graveyard to my hand as the 
number of monsters I tributed!

00:21:05.070 --> 00:21:07.840
I return two Nimble Momongas!

00:21:09.020 --> 00:21:12.460
I switch Nimble Momonga on 
my field to attack position!

00:21:19.020 --> 00:21:21.520
This is very bad.

00:21:21.520 --> 00:21:25.490
Yusei will lose if he 
takes those three attacks.

00:21:25.800 --> 00:21:26.720
Yusei.

00:21:27.000 --> 00:21:27.960
Yusei!

00:21:29.920 --> 00:21:35.530
If he beats him so easily, we won't 
be able to see his strategies.

00:21:36.560 --> 00:21:39.400
What will you do, Yusei Fudo?

00:22:07.960 --> 00:22:12.950
The small cliff floats on the Milky Way

00:22:12.950 --> 00:22:17.830
The sights I see are different 
than what I imagined

00:22:17.830 --> 00:22:22.770
Were you able to move on from the past?

00:22:22.770 --> 00:22:27.780
The answer isn't no, but 
there's something missing

00:22:27.780 --> 00:22:32.830
The cruel god tests us

00:22:32.830 --> 00:22:39.390
Let's fill the emptiness 
and head to the next stage

00:22:39.390 --> 00:22:43.460
If you ask me "What's our relationship?"

00:22:43.460 --> 00:22:49.300
We're more than friends... 
but that's not quite right

00:22:49.300 --> 00:22:53.390
Bond is the proper word

00:22:53.390 --> 00:22:59.010
As we fight, we understand each other

00:22:59.010 --> 00:23:02.190
"Where are you right now?"  "On Earth"

00:23:02.190 --> 00:23:04.450
Because I'm not an astronaut

00:23:04.450 --> 00:23:08.980
I have no problems when 
I'm below the ozone layer

00:23:08.980 --> 00:23:11.950
"I know, I'm coming right away."

00:23:11.950 --> 00:23:15.390
You want to party until the morning

00:23:15.390 --> 00:23:18.770
At our special place
